flowchart LR
    %% Data Flow Diagram for Option 3: Translation-as-a-Service (TaaS)
    
    subgraph Velocity Domain [🟩 Velocity Bounded Context]
        direction TB
        V_App[Velocity Origination App]
        V_Topic[(Velocity Native Topic)]
        V_Repo[Velocity Git Repo <br/> mapping.jsonata]
        
        V_App -->|1. Publishes Native Event| V_Topic
    end

    subgraph Mosaic Domain [🟦 Mosaic Bounded Context]
        direction TB
        M_App[Mosaic Servicing App]
        M_Topic[(Mosaic Native Topic)]
        M_Repo[Mosaic Git Repo <br/> mapping.jsonata]
        
        M_App -->|1. Publishes Native Event| M_Topic
    end

    subgraph TaaS Platform [⚙️ Stand-Alone TaaS Platform]
        direction TB
        GitOps[CI/CD GitOps Pipeline <br/> Validation & Deployment]
        Engine[[Centralized Translation Engine <br/> Stateless]]
        
        V_Repo -.->|2. Commits Rules| GitOps
        M_Repo -.->|2. Commits Rules| GitOps
        GitOps -.->|3. Loads Validated Config| Engine
        
        V_Topic -->|4. Consumes Native Event| Engine
        M_Topic -->|4. Consumes Native Event| Engine
    end

    subgraph Data Domain [🟧 Enterprise Data Domain]
        direction TB
        HubProxy[InteractionHub <br/> Kafka REST Proxy]
        EntTopic[(Enterprise Canonical Topic)]
        ODS[(Enterprise ODS)]
        
        HubProxy -->|6. Produces Record to| EntTopic
        EntTopic -->|7. Ingests via Sink Connector| ODS
    end

    %% Cross-Domain Translation Flows
    Engine -->|5. HTTP POST Canonical JSON| HubProxy

